## 28. Final Methodological Principle

The codebook enforces the following analytical discipline: do not ask only what countries have or where they participate. Ask how capabilities are mobilised, whether actors form a tractable coalition, through which mechanisms and instruments they coordinate, where leverage can be exercised, what conditions shape the process, and whether an observable governance effect follows.

The analysis should allow the researcher to reconstruct the following sequence: capability, coalition, coordination, institutionalisation, leverage point, and governance effect, conditioned throughout by structural and institutional conditions.

The codebook is designed to remain compact enough for consistent manual application across the six cases. Its priority is analytical consistency, evidentiary traceability, and comparative usefulness, rather than exhaustive coding.
